        "v": 5,
        "title": "Remove fingerprintid column from message table schema",
        "summary": "Migration 0026 drops the `fingerprint_id` column, its foreign key constraint, and associated index from the `message` table. The `insertMessageRecord` function in `message-cost-tracker.ts` no longer writes `fingerprint_id` to the database. This change affects the backend cost tracking logic and the shared database schema definitions.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T10:19:10.987Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you look at a message record or a trace of an API call, you'll no longer see a fingerprint ID attached to it. The database column that stored this anonymous identifier has been permanently removed, and the code that used to write it there no longer does. The backend systems that relied on linking messages through this ID (including a script that counts daily active users) have been updated to work without it. This affects anyone viewing message traces or running analytics that depended on that identifier. The change is live today.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
