        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add --agent flag to evals",
        "summary": "Added `--agent` flag to `run-eval-set` command, defaulting to 'base'. Replaced hardcoded `agentType` in `EvalConfig` with dynamic `agent` value passed through `runGitEvals` and `run-single-eval-process`. Updates `agent_model` in `GitEvalResultRequest` to use this new flag. Scope: `evals/git-evals` subsystem.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T10:12:52.661Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You can now pick which version of the coding agent runs an evaluation by passing a new --agent option (for example, --agent base). Previously the agent type was set in a fixed configuration that couldn't be changed per run. This lets evaluation operators direct each test to a specific agent build instead of always using the default. The option defaults to 'base' if none is provided, so existing workflows continue to run as before.",
